    id:'leslie-danville-1860-index-page-audit', people:['mft-f6fb8b50-1694-442a-94a8-891dedb0d817'], title:'No Leslie spelling surfaced in the Hendricks 1860 township indexes', confidence:'provisional', sourceKind:'archival index',
    citation:'United States Census, 1860, Indiana, Hendricks County FamilySearch browse Image Index, NARA M653 reel 265; reviewed all 17 listed township/place sets on 6 October 2026: Brownsburg 4 images, Brown Township 50, Center 35, Clay 30, Danville 23, Eel River 4, Edriver 31, Franklin 29, Guilford 42, Liberty 45, Marian 31, Middle 35, New Winchester 4, North Salem 3, North Salem Ed River Township 1, Union 24, Washington 36. Visible names on each image-index page were checked for Leslie, Lesley, Lasley, Lashley, Lassley and Tillman variants; no candidate surfaced. Total 427 image-index pages. A separate FamilySearch 1860 collection query for surname Lashley and residence Hendricks County, selected from the place autocomplete, returned zero results. Original schedules are browsable in the same collection.',
    url:'https://www.familysearch.org/en/search/collection/1473181',
    finding:'All 17 FamilySearch Hendricks County township/place browse sets were reviewed page by page, covering 427 image-index pages. None surfaced Leslie, Lesley, Lasley, Lashley or Lassley name strings or an indexed Tillman candidate. The browse index therefore does not corroborate the 1850 Danville Lasley candidates, despite the separate 1860 voters transcription listing J.G. Lashley in Center Township.',
    limit:'This exhaustive pass covers the derivative FamilySearch image index, not a transcription of all 427 handwritten census schedule pages. Index coverage can omit or misread names; the separate voter-list discrepancy demonstrates why the zero image-index result cannot establish absence. Age-compatible unidentified boys and a name-change or migration remain possible. No identity exclusion or family relationship conclusion follows.',
    next:'Use the uncatalogued-by-name original NARA M653 reel 265 schedules to test John/Eliza Lasley and the age-compatible Tillman/James candidates township by township. If a household is found, compare its full composition and birthplaces to the 1850 and 1870 records; otherwise keep the connection unresolved and prioritize independent death/marriage records.'
